1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,650
It’s great to see so many members of the Twinning Association here tonight.

2
00:00:06,650 --> 00:00:12,161
Since the twinning link between our two towns, Stanthorpe here in England

3
00:00:12,161 --> 00:00:20,078
and Malatte in France, was established,the relationship between the towns has gone from strength

4
00:00:20,078 --> 00:00:21,120
to strength.

5
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:28,900
Last month, 25 members of the association from Stanthorpe spent a weekend in Malatte.

6
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:32,700
Our hosts had arranged a great programme.

7
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:37,381
We learned how cheese is produced in the region and had the chance to

8
00:00:37,381 --> 00:00:39,270
taste the products.

9
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:42,201
The theme park trip had to be cancelled,

10
00:00:42,201 --> 00:00:46,757
but we all had a great time on the final boat trip down the

11
00:00:46,757 --> 00:00:50,250
river – that was the real highlight.

12
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:56,804
This is a special year for the Association because it’s 25 years since we

13
00:00:56,804 --> 00:00:58,050
were founded.

14
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:04,850
In Malatte, they’re planning to mark this by building a footbridge in the municipal

15
00:01:04,850 --> 00:01:04,900
park.

16
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:11,153
We’ve been discussing what to do here and we’ve decided to plant a poplar

17
00:01:11,153 --> 00:01:13,120
tree in the museum gardens.

18
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:16,438
We considered buying a garden seat to put there,

19
00:01:16,438 --> 00:01:20,520
but the authorities weren’t happy with that idea.

20
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:26,870
In terms of fundraising to support our activities, we’ve done very well.

21
00:01:26,870 --> 00:01:32,062
Our pancake evening was well attended and made record profits.

22
00:01:32,062 --> 00:01:37,005
And everyone enjoyed the demonstration of French cookery,

23
00:01:37,005 --> 00:01:39,820
which was nearly as successful.

24
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:44,649
Numbers for our film show were limited because of the venue

25
00:01:44,649 --> 00:01:48,600
so we’re looking for somewhere bigger next year.

26
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:53,631
We’re looking forward to welcoming our French visitors here next week,

27
00:01:53,631 --> 00:01:59,500
and I know that many of you here will be hosting individuals or families.

28
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:05,100
The coach from France will arrive at 5 pm on Friday.

29
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:10,529
Don’t try to do too much that first evening as they’ll be

30
00:02:10,529 --> 00:02:10,917
tired,

31
00:02:10,917 --> 00:02:15,570
so have dinner in the house or garden rather than eating out.

32
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:21,041
The weather looks as if it’ll be OK so you might like to plan

33
00:02:21,041 --> 00:02:21,770
a barbecue.

34
00:02:21,770 --> 00:02:25,645
Then the next morning’s market day in town,

35
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:29,950
and that’s always a good place to stroll round.

36
00:02:29,950 --> 00:02:38,262
On Saturday evening, we’ll all meet up at the footballclub, where once again we’ll have Toby Sharp

37
00:02:38,262 --> 00:02:42,200
and his band performing English and Scottish country songs.

38
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:52,237
Toby will already be well known to many of you as last year he organised our special quiz night

39
00:02:52,237 --> 00:02:54,350
and presented the prizes.

40
00:02:54,350 --> 00:02:58,669
Now on Sunday, we’ll betaking our visitors to Farley House.

41
00:02:58,669 --> 00:03:01,809
You may not all be familiar with it,

42
00:03:01,809 --> 00:03:04,950
so here’s a map to help you.

43
00:03:04,950 --> 00:03:10,672
You can see the car park at the bottom of the map.There’s an excellent

44
00:03:10,672 --> 00:03:15,679
farm shop in the grounds where our visitors can buy local produce – it’s

45
00:03:15,679 --> 00:03:19,970
in the old stables,which is the first building you come to.

46
00:03:19,970 --> 00:03:22,176
They’re built round a courtyard,

47
00:03:22,176 --> 00:03:26,220
and the shop’s in the far corner on the left.

48
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:31,200
There’s also a small café on the right as you go in.

49
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:36,520
I know that one or two of our visitors may not be all that

50
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:36,900
mobile.

51
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:41,008
The main entrance to the house has a lot of steps

52
00:03:41,008 --> 00:03:44,370
so you might want to use the disabled entry.

53
00:03:44,370 --> 00:03:49,120
This is on the far side of the house from the car park.

54
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:54,250
Children will probably be most interested in the adventure playground.

55
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:59,479
That’s at the northern end of the larger lake, in a bend on the

56
00:03:59,479 --> 00:04:01,570
path that leads to the lake.

57
00:04:01,570 --> 00:04:08,730
There’s lots for children to do there.There are a number of lovely gardens near

58
00:04:08,730 --> 00:04:09,625
the house.

59
00:04:09,625 --> 00:04:14,100
The kitchen gardens are rectangular and surrounded by a wall.

60
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:19,020
They’re to the north-east of the house, quite near the smaller lake.

61
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:24,870
They’re still in use and have a great collection of fruit and vegetables.

62
00:04:24,870 --> 00:04:29,167
The Temple of the Four Winds is a bit more of a walk –

63
00:04:29,167 --> 00:04:30,820
but it’s worth it.

64
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:37,161
Take the path from the car park and go past the western sides of the stables

65
00:04:37,161 --> 00:04:38,350
and the house.

66
00:04:38,350 --> 00:04:42,043
Then when the path forks, take the right-hand path.

67
00:04:42,043 --> 00:04:47,789
Go up there with the woods on your left and the temple is right

68
00:04:47,789 --> 00:04:49,020
at the end.

69
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:52,673
There are great views over the whole area.

70
00:04:52,673 --> 00:04:53,130
OK,

71
00:04:53,130 --> 00:04:54,500
so that’s .

72
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:54,550
.

73
00:04:54,550 --> 00:04:54,600
.
